#Plan for Course Project
This section explains my plan for completing the project using both the Elite College Admissions dataset and the 2025 SAT Suite Annual Report.
For this project, my plan was to analyze the relationship between household income, SAT performance, and elite college admissions.
I first reviewed the Elite College Admissions dataset from the CMU Statistics & Data Science Data Repository.
I then reviewed the 2025 Total Group SAT Suite of Assessments Annual Report to understand national SAT trends.
I identified key variables related to household income and elite college admission status in the CMU dataset.
I identified SAT score and income-related tables in the SAT Suite report.
I imported the Elite College Admissions dataset into R for analysis.
I extracted and imported relevant SAT summary tables into R.
I cleaned and organized both datasets to ensure consistent variable names and formats.
I summarized household income distributions and elite college admission rates.
I summarized national SAT participation and average scores by income group.
I compared patterns in SAT performance with elite college admission outcomes.
I created simple charts to show relationships between income, SAT scores, and elite admissions.
I wrote short explanations describing what each result showed.
I kept most of the code in a separate section so the main report focused on results.
I rendered the Quarto document to make sure the analysis worked correctly.
